## Appendix A. Additional learning components

**A.1 Queue forecasting (supervised).** Per-lane queues (halting vehicles) were logged every second
from eight training-seed episodes (fixed-time, max-pressure and PPO control, four scenarios) and
evaluated on four held-out-seed episodes: [[forecast.meta.n_train_windows:int]] training and
[[forecast.meta.n_test_windows:int]] test windows. Inputs: the last [[forecast.meta.history_s]] s of
all 12 lane queues plus the phase one-hot; targets: each lane's queue 30 s and 60 s ahead. MAE in
vehicles (95 % bootstrap CIs over held-out episodes): last value
[[forecast.last_value.h30.mae:.2f]] / [[forecast.last_value.h60.mae:.2f]]
([[forecast.last_value.h60.mae_ci_low:.2f]] to [[forecast.last_value.h60.mae_ci_high:.2f]] at 60 s),
moving average [[forecast.moving_average.h30.mae:.2f]] / [[forecast.moving_average.h60.mae:.2f]],
GRU [[forecast.gru.h30.mae:.2f]] / [[forecast.gru.h60.mae:.2f]]
([[forecast.gru.h60.mae_ci_low:.2f]] to [[forecast.gru.h60.mae_ci_high:.2f]] at 60 s),
TCN [[forecast.tcn.h30.mae:.2f]] / [[forecast.tcn.h60.mae:.2f]]
([[forecast.tcn.h60.mae_ci_low:.2f]] to [[forecast.tcn.h60.mae_ci_high:.2f]] at 60 s).
RMSE at 60 s: last value [[forecast.last_value.h60.rmse:.2f]], GRU [[forecast.gru.h60.rmse:.2f]],
TCN [[forecast.tcn.h60.rmse:.2f]]. Both networks roughly halve the error of the naive baselines at
both horizons; the GRU and the TCN are within each other's confidence intervals. The
forecast-augmented PPO variant (forecasts appended to the observation) was not trained within the
budget.

![Queue forecasting error by model and horizon](../figures/forecast_mae.png)

**A.2 Imitation-learning warm start.** [[imitation.bc_ppo.bc_samples:int]] (observation, mask,
action) tuples from the max-pressure controller on training seeds were used to train the policy MLP
by masked cross-entropy (held-out accuracy [[imitation.bc_ppo.bc_val_acc:.3f]]); the cloned weights
and the dataset's observation statistics initialise MaskablePPO. With the same seed, budget and
hyper-parameters, the validation return at the first evaluation is
[[imitation.ppo_scratch.first_return:.0f]] from scratch vs [[imitation.bc_ppo.first_return:.0f]] with
the warm start, at 100k steps [[imitation.ppo_scratch.return_at_100k:.0f]] vs
[[imitation.bc_ppo.return_at_100k:.0f]], and the best validation return is
[[imitation.ppo_scratch.best:.0f]] (full run) vs [[imitation.bc_ppo.best:.0f]] (the warm-started
run was interrupted by a VM restart after 245k of 300k steps, so its curve is compared on the
overlapping window only).

![Learning curves: PPO from scratch vs behaviour-cloning warm start](../figures/imitation_curves.png)

**A.3 Graph coordination on the 2x2 grid.** The `grid2x2` network, the parameter-shared
multi-junction environment, the neighbour-observation layout and the graph-attention encoder
(`src/drs/gnn.py`) are implemented and unit-tested, and three variant configs exist
(`configs/train_grid_{independent,shared,gnn}.yaml`), but the grid runs were **not executed** for the
same reason as A.1. No grid numbers are reported.
